#. front matter: title
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:2 site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:5
msgid "3. Lists (basics), tuples and sets"
msgstr "3. Lists (основи), tuples и sets"

#. html
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:8
msgid "<span>Session 3</span><span>practice: <code>03-lists-tuples-sets/</code> in the homework repository</span>"
msgstr "<span>Занятие 3</span><span>упражнения: <code>03-lists-tuples-sets/</code> в homework repository</span>"

#. html
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:9
msgid "<span><a href=\"../sample-data\">the sample data</a></span>"
msgstr "<span><a href=\"../sample-data\">примерните данни</a></span>"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:12
msgid "**Today you will learn to:**"
msgstr "**Днес ще се научите да:**"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:14
msgid "keep many values in one **list**, and read them by index (from 0!) and by slices;"
msgstr "пазите много стойности в един **list** и да ги четете по индекс (от 0!) и със slices;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:15
msgid "use the operations that all sequences share: `+`, `*`, `in`, `len`, `min`, `max`;"
msgstr "използвате операциите, общи за всички поредици: `+`, `*`, `in`, `len`, `min`, `max`;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:16
msgid "change a list with its methods, and sort it;"
msgstr "променяте list с неговите методи и да го сортирате;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:17
msgid "understand why two names can show the same list - and how to make a copy;"
msgstr "разбирате защо две имена могат да показват един и същ list - и как да направите копие;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:18
msgid "use **tuples** as records that cannot change, and unpack them;"
msgstr "използвате **tuples** като записи, които не могат да се променят, и да ги разопаковате;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:19
msgid "use `range` for sequences of numbers;"
msgstr "използвате `range` за поредици от числа;"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:20
msgid "find unique values with **sets**, and compare groups the way SQL `UNION`, `INTERSECT` and `EXCEPT` do - the Python way."
msgstr "намирате уникалните стойности със **sets** и да сравнявате групи като `UNION`, `INTERSECT` и `EXCEPT` в SQL - по начина на Python."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:23
msgid "From SQL to Python - the same question, two ways. Which clients have no loans?"
msgstr "От SQL към Python - един и същ въпрос, по два начина. Кои клиенти нямат кредити?"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:49
msgid "1. Sequences"
msgstr "1. Поредици"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:51
msgid "What is a sequence?"
msgstr "Какво е поредица (sequence)?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:53
msgid "[Session 2](./02-conditions-and-loops.md#_12-the-for-loop) used `for` on strings, lists and ranges. They are all **sequences**: containers that keep an **ordered** collection of values. The main sequence types:"
msgstr "В [занятие 2](./02-conditions-and-loops.md#_12-the-for-loop) използвахме `for` върху strings, lists и ranges. Всички те са **поредици** (sequences): контейнери, които пазят **подредена** колекция от стойности. Основните типове поредици:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:56
msgid "Type"
msgstr "Тип"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:56 site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:87
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Пример"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:56
msgid "Can it change?"
msgstr "Може ли да се променя?"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:58
msgid "yes"
msgstr "да"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:59 site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:60 site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:61 site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:988
msgid "no"
msgstr "не"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:73
msgid "Every item of a sequence has a number - its position, or **index**. The index **starts from 0**."
msgstr "Всеки елемент на поредицата има номер - своята позиция, или **индекс**. Индексът **започва от 0**."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:76
msgid "Python counts from 0, SAS from 1"
msgstr "Python брои от 0, SAS - от 1"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:77
msgid "The first character of a string: `SUBSTR(loan_id, 1, 1)` in SAS and SQL, but `loan_id[0]` in Python. The first element of a SAS array is `arr{1}`; of a Python list it is `items[0]`. This is the most common mistake in the first weeks - count with care."
msgstr "Първият символ на string: `SUBSTR(loan_id, 1, 1)` в SAS и SQL, но `loan_id[0]` в Python. Първият елемент на SAS array е `arr{1}`; на Python list е `items[0]`. Това е най-честата грешка през първите седмици - броете внимателно."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:83
msgid "What all sequences can do"
msgstr "Какво могат всички поредици"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-lists-tuples-sets.md:85
msgid "All sequences support the same **common operations** - you learn them once:"
msgstr "Всички поредици поддържат едни и същи **общи операции** - учите ги веднъж:"

